<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal ind prod falls 3.3 pct yr/yr in Dec.</title>
<headline>Portugal ind prod falls 3.3 pct yr/yr in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's index of industrial production fell 3.3 percent year-on-year in December 1996, while month-on-month it fell 5.1 percent, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>					 Dec 96	Nov 95	Dec 95</p>
<p>General Index			 97.8	  103.1	101.1</p>
<p>Percentage change yr/yr	   -3.3	  -0.7</p>
<p>Percentage change mo/mo	   -5.3	  -0.8</p>
<p>Accumulated 12 months	     +0.7	  +1.7</p>
<p>Base Year = 1990  </p>
<p>Mining				  98.7	   85.4	100.5</p>
<p>Manufacturing industry	    92.8	  102.1	 87.3</p>
<p>Energy production		  119.5	  111.0	161.3</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
